  "cardTextTail": "suggestion\nprose\nauto-apply\npending\n\nPresent-perfect verb \"has changed\" clashes with surrounding past-tense narration (\"She let them sit\"), creating a small consistency stumble within the opening simile.\n\nChapter 1\n\nShow diff\nJump to text\nApply\nDismiss\nHide\nPROSE\n\nThe tense shift is not deliberate here — I just missed it. Show me your tighter version of that sentence so I can compare.\n\nHere is the adjusted sentence matching your narrative past.\n\nAI Rewrite Comparison\nprose\n+0 words\n\nORIGINAL (24 WORDS)\n\nShe let them sit, the way you let a burn sit before you touch it again, testing whether the pain has changed its mind.\n\nAI REWRITE (24 WORDS)\n\nShe let them sit, the way you let a burn sit before you touch it again, testing whether the pain had changed its mind.\n\nHide diff\nEdit\nReject\nAccept Rewrite\n\nUnderstood. In one sentence, what would you watch for in the rest of the chapter if I take that fix?\n\nWatch for other accidental tense slips, especially inside embedded similes or interior parentheticals.\n\nUse it\nKeep as-is",
